# Looped's first words (J116.2; the language: looped/words/words.h).
#
# Every word is a small script made of other words (request 2026-10-27
# #10, #11). Its first line says what kind of word it is; the lines under
# it are its meaning; `like:` links it to words it's close to (for hints,
# and the map of words). Change a word here and everything made with it
# changes. The engine itself gives only the roots: the settings (lumens,
# colour, brightness, amount, every, speed), the units, the shapes (wave,
# noise, flicker, thump) and what a thing can be made of (a model, a box,
# a light).

# ---- Things that give light ----

word light: a thing
  gives light: 100 lumens, 2700 K, a ball 5 cm across
  like: lamp, glow, shine

word bulb: a thing, a kind of light
  made of a box 6 by 6 by 9 cm
  glows warm white
  gives light: 200 lumens, 2700 K, a ball 6 cm across
  like: lamp, light, globe

word flame: a thing, a kind of light
  gives light: 12 lumens, 1800 K, a ball 1 cm across
  flickering
  like: fire, candle, blaze

word candle: a thing
  made of the model candle.glb
  has a flame 9 cm above it
  like: flame, wax, wick

word pendant lamp: a thing
  made of the model pendant_lamp.glb
  has a bulb 80 cm below it
  like: lamp, shade, ceiling light

word neon tube: a thing
  made of a box 100 by 3 by 3 cm
  glows pink
  gives light: 120 lumens, colour 1 0.25 0.6, a tube 1 m long
  buzzing
  like: neon, sign, tube

word sign: a thing
  made of a box 100 by 3 by 30 cm
  glows blue
  gives light: 150 lumens, colour 0.3 0.8 1, a panel 1 by 0.3 m, from one side
  like: neon, poster, signboard

# ---- Things that don't ----

word table: a thing
  made of the model round_table.glb
  like: desk, counter

word stool: a thing
  made of the model table_stool.glb
  like: seat, chair, bench

# ---- Describing a light ----

word warm: describes a light
  colour down 300 K
  like: cozy, cosy, golden, amber, sunset, fire

word cool: describes a light
  colour up 1500 K
  like: cold, daylight, crisp

word white: describes a light
  colour 4000 K
  like: plain, clean

word red: describes a light
  colour 1 0.15 0.1
  like: crimson, scarlet

word pink: describes a light
  colour 1 0.25 0.6
  like: magenta, rose

word blue: describes a light
  colour 0.3 0.6 1
  like: azure, sky, navy

word green: describes a light
  colour 0.3 1 0.4
  like: lime, emerald

word bright: describes a light
  lumens times 2
  like: strong, vivid, intense

word dim: describes a light
  lumens times 0.4
  like: faint, low, weak, soft

word soft: describes a light
  size times 3
  like: gentle, diffuse, hazy

# ---- Describing a doing ----

word fast: describes a doing
  every times 0.5
  like: quick, rapid, hurried

word slow: describes a doing
  every times 2
  like: lazy, calm, leisurely

word gently: describes a doing
  amount times 0.5
  like: softly, lightly, subtly

word wildly: describes a doing
  amount times 2
  like: strongly, madly, hard

# ---- How much ----

word very: an amount
  times 2
  like: really, extremely

word a little: an amount
  times 0.5
  like: slightly, somewhat

word slightly: an amount
  times 0.5

# ---- Doings (what a light does over time) ----

word flicker (flickers, flickering): a doing
  settings: amount 30%, every 0.5 s, speed 1
  brightness times 1 + amount * flicker(period every, speed speed)
  like: shimmer, waver, gutter

word buzz (buzzes, buzzing): a doing
  settings: amount 12%, every 2 s, speed 0.8
  brightness times 1 + amount * flicker(period every, speed speed)
  like: hum, fizz

word breathe (breathes, breathing): a doing
  settings: amount 6%, every 8 s, speed 0.5
  brightness times 1 + amount * noise(period every, speed speed)
  like: pulse, swell

word wave (waves, waving): a doing
  settings: amount 18%, every 5 s
  brightness times 1 + amount * wave(period every)
  like: sway, ripple

word pulse (pulses, pulsing): a doing
  settings: amount 70%, every 1 beat, fade 7
  brightness times 1 - amount / 3 + amount * thump(period every, fade fade)
  like: beat, throb, thump
